<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Boa Vista launches note program.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Boa Vista launches note program.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Banco Boa Vista is launching a $100 million 180-day trade note program through Bank of America, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Due to high demand, Boa Vista upped its first tranche to $80 million from $50 million, it said. The remaining $20 million will be placed throughout the rest of the year.</p>
<p>The money will be used to finance trade operations for Boa Vista clients with gross revenues of betweem $5 million and $50 million, the statement said.</p>
<p>--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 232-4411</p>
</text>
